    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I grew up seeing math as a tool for problem-solving more than an abstract subject—something my father often used to explain physics and engineering concepts. While I didn’t excel at it, its logic felt satisfying when I could apply it to real-world scenarios, like calculating costs in games or painting proportions. It’s not something I’d call fun, but I’ve developed a practical curiosity rather than fear.",
